{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjaE4kSQ7SnHkF5TY2gM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TxRMtsM8GxYcQgLkZhjeZe","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"working":"The line has five bars. Each has eight slurred eighths in pairs. Bar 1 of the line: low-high pairs (Eb4 G4) ×4, with \"R.\" under the third pair. That is bar 126, which has [rf] on its third pair. Bar 125 would have [fp] at the start instead. Bar 2: high-low pairs (F4 D4) ×4, with \"P.\" under the third pair. That is bar 127. Bar 3: (F4 D4) ×4, with \"R.\" at the start and \"P.\" under the third pair. That is bar 128, which has rf at the start and p on the third pair. Bar 4: (Eb4 G4) ×4 with no dynamics. That is bar 129. Bar 5: (Eb4 G4) ×4 with no dynamic marked. That is bar 130; the edition's [rf] on its third pair is missing here, but the pitches match. The line ends there with a barline. Bars 131–133 are not on this line: (F4 D4) ×2, then the Eb4 half.","right":false,"insights":"The line is easy to match from two things: the pattern of pairs (EG, FD, FD, EG, EG) and the copyist's R./P. marks. The R./P. marks pin bars 126–128 exactly. The program's end, bar 133, ran three bars past the five barlines. Counting the bars against the edition, or seeing that the line has no half-note ending, would have caught it."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5299,"cache_read_input_tokens":523,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5299},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7456591-0e8c-44c4-ad2d-c4c719412a6e","uuid":"813cdb4c-af2c-475c-a9f4-cc28cfb76257","timestamp":"2026-11-05T09:50:43.890Z","request_id":"req_011Cg